# Unlike the suites above, this directory tracks nothing it generates -- not the
# score tables either. Only the script that rebuilds them is kept.
figures/simplex3_qwen-05temp/*
!figures/simplex3_qwen-05temp/make_temperature_figures.py
!figures/simplex3_qwen-05temp/make_temperature_curves.py

docs/notes/

# The per-shard configs and sbatch scripts. `scripts/gen_simplex3.py --suite <s>`
# writes them, they differ from one another only in a shard number and a strided
# slice of the adapter list, and there are 888 of them across thirteen trees --
# enough to bury every hand-written file in `experiments/` and `jobs/` in a diff.
# The generator, the Suite and the DataSimplexSpec stay tracked, so the tree is
# still reproducible from one command; what is no longer tracked is its output.
experiments/*/*_shard*.yaml
jobs/*/*_shard*.sh
**shard**.sh
figures/simplex_collection_size/.fanout/

# Generated greedy shard configs for figures/simplex_collection_size;
# regenerate with figures/simplex_collection_size/make_greedy_shards.py
experiments/simplex_collection_size_greedy/

# The nsweep tree, whole. Every file in it is written by
# `scripts/gen_simplex3.py --suite olmo2_nsweep` -- 54 train shards, 40
# behavioral shards, and the handful of non-shard drivers beside them -- so
# unlike the older suites there is nothing hand-written left to keep. The two
# rules above would leave the drivers tracked; these ignore the directories.
experiments/simplex3_nsweep_*/
jobs/simplex3_nsweep_*/

# Run logs from the nsweep scoring sweep. The CSV it writes is the artifact;
# these are just the per-slice progress lines.
figures/simplex3_nsweep_olmo2_nsweep/logs/
